+## Live stunt score
+
+Option (General > Gameplay, Live Stunt Score, on by default). The trick box (the left half of the stunt score panel,
+on stunt tracks and with Stunts on All Tracks) normally shows a trick only once the car lands, so a trick lost to a
+wreck was never shown. With the option on it shows what the trick under way would score if the car landed now.
+
+**Scoring.** `car_stunt_scoring_update_80065588` (called by `car_sound_update_all_80067358` for each player slot,
+only while the car isn't wrecked, car +0x648 == 0) keeps one trick per slot, in s32 [2] arrays:
+
+| Address | Holds |
+| --- | --- |
+| 0x800E7D08 | airborne: set when all four wheels are off the ground (car +0x60C, +0x60E, +0x610, +0x612 == 8) |
+| 0x800E7D58 | f32 takeoff time |
+| 0x800E7DE8 | f32 time a wheel first touched down again, -1 until then |
+| 0x800E7CB8 | phase of the current rotation, from the car's up vector y (car +0x2DC): 0 upright, 1 below 0, 2 below -0.5; 0, 1, 2, 1, 0 is one turn over, counted only with all four wheels up |
+| 0x800E7D28 | turns completed |
+| 0x800E7D40 | turns completed after a wheel had touched down (0x800E7DE8 set) |
+| 0x800E7DF8 | on two wheels: one side's wheels down (0 and 2, or 1 and 3) |
+| 0x800E7E08, 0x800E7E18 | f32 times the two-wheel run started and ended (-1 while it goes on) |
+
+The car lands with three or four wheels down. Each kind that scored adds points and counts once toward the
+multiplier, and the score is points x kinds:
+
+| Kind | Flag | Scores when | Points |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| 2 WHEELS | 1 | on two wheels for 1 s or more | (t - 0.75) / 0.25 |
+| AIR TIME | 2 | more than 5 s from takeoff to first touch | (int)t - 4 |
+| FLIPS | 4 | turns done with all four wheels up | one each |
+| ROLLS | 8 | turns done after a wheel touched down | one each |
+
+`car_stunt_award_80065270` (slot, flags, points, kinds) puts it in the box and adds points x kinds to the TOTAL
+(0x8010C074, u16 [2]) and BEST (0x8010C068, u8 [2]). The box's variables: 0x8010C070 u8 [2] shown, 0x8010C0D8 f32 [2]
+time shown (relocated to 0x80240730 for four players), 0x8010C0B4 s8 [2] points, 0x8010C0C0 s8 [2] kinds and
+0x8010C0D4 u8 [2] the name (0 2 WHEELS, 1 AIR TIME, 2 FLIPS, 3 ROLLS, 4 COMBO when more than one kind; English names
+at 0x800C4BAC). A wreck goes through `func_8006722C`, which clears slots 0 and 1's airborne and two-wheel flags
+(`car_stunt_reset_800671E8`), so the trick scores nothing.
+
+**Drawing.** `hud_widget_text_cb_player_stats_800B7654` draws, for each slot whose shown byte is set and whose time
+is less than 2.75 s old, the name centered at x 0x4A and the points under it (`"%s X%i"` with the kinds when more than
+one), then BEST and TOTAL on the right. Its first frame (widget +0x30 < 0) clears the shown bytes and the totals.
+
+**The option.** The hook at 0x800B772C (`rush2_stunt_live_score`), where that first-frame reset joins the drawing
+path and before the player loop, works out each of players 1 and 2's trick as the landing would with now as the
+landing time and, when it would score, writes it into the box's variables with the time now. The totals are left
+alone. After a wreck the last preview stays for the box's 2.75 s; a landing writes the real score over it.
+
